id: pm-rizqb6
title: "A single transient per-test timeout fails the whole pipeline: 1,942 tests share one uniform 30s budget, no retry is configured, and the only diagnosis path is decoding a blob artifact"
description: ""
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: ci,diagnostics,flake,reliability,testing
created_at: "2026-08-13T09:13:18.162Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-14T01:03:20.026Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-14T01:03:19.416Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-14T01:03:19.416Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: "A transient test failure is retried a bounded number of times and the retry is recorded, so a single timeout cannot fail the pipeline on its own; Flake occurrences are recorded with test identity, duration and shard so recurrence is a number that can be watched rather than a memory of having seen it before; Per-test timeout budgets are derived from or checked against observed per-test cost, so a test running near its budget is reported as at-risk before it crosses it under load; The failing test name and error appear in the job summary without decoding the coverage blob artifact; A negative control proves a genuinely failing assertion still fails after retries and is never classified as a flake"
goal: explainable-graph
objective: "A transient failure is distinguishable from a real one before it reddens the default branch, and the distinction is recorded rather than re-derived by a human rerun"
value: "Every red run that turns out to be transient trains the next reader to rerun first and diagnose second, which is exactly the habit that lets a real regression through."
impact: "A tracker-only commit that changes no source file can and did fail CI, so the signal that gates the release path is not currently attributable to the change that triggered it."
outcome: Transient timeouts are retried and recorded as flakes with their test identity and duration; a test whose cost approaches its budget is reported before it crosses it; the failing test name is visible without downloading an artifact.
why_now: "Observed live on commit 1cc62476d, a tracker-and-CHANGELOG-only commit: shard 1 of 4 failed with one timeout out of 1,942 tests while the same file passes locally in 24s for all 30 tests."
parent: pm-33cw
risk: medium
confidence: 90
resolution: "CI retries each failed test once, records flaky and near-timeout evidence in isolated per-shard artifacts, annotates failures, and keeps persistent failures terminal."
expected_result: "A transient test failure receives one recorded retry with identity, duration, and shard evidence; reliability diagnostics never enter Vitest blob aggregation; a genuine persistent failure still fails visibly."
actual_result: All hosted coverage shards pass with the reporter; isolated artifact namespaces prevent aggregate parser collisions; executable transient/persistent and workflow contract controls pass.
