close_reason: Bounded retry diagnostics and isolated reliability artifacts verified locally and against hosted shard execution.
body: "## The observed failure\n\nRun 31684928972, workflow CI, commit `1cc62476d` on main. That commit changes only `.agents/pm/**` and the generated `CHANGELOG.md`; no file under `src/`, `scripts/`, `docs/` or `.github/` is touched.\n\n```\nFAIL tests/unit/commands/test-all-command.spec.ts > runTestAll >\n     treats per-test pm_context_mode metadata as part of dedupe identity\nError: Test timed out in 30000ms.\nTest Files  1 failed | 122 passed (123)\n     Tests  1 failed | 1941 passed (1942)\n  Duration  86.90s (transform 16.96s, import 49.51s, tests 166.57s)\n```\n\nEvery other job on the commit passed: CodeQL, CodSpeed, Docs, Security and Script Quality, OSSF Scorecard, and coverage shards 2, 3 and 4.\n\n## Local reproduction attempt\n\n`node scripts/run-tests.mjs test -- tests/unit/commands/test-all-command.spec.ts` passes all 30 tests in the file in 24.30s, tests 21.19s. The heaviest test in the file takes 4,038ms. The test uses `withTempPmPath`, so it operates on a sandboxed tracker and is structurally independent of the tracker data the commit changed.\n\nSo the failure is a timeout under load, not a defect the commit introduced.\n\n## The configuration that turns one timeout into a red branch\n\n`vitest.config.ts` declares `testTimeout: 30_000` and `hookTimeout: 30_000`. There is no `retry` setting, so vitest's default of zero applies. The shard job has `timeout-minutes: 12` and the run itself took 86.9s, so the job was nowhere near its own limit; the per-test budget was the binding constraint.\n\nThe budget is uniform across all 1,942 tests. Most complete in hundreds of milliseconds. A handful spawn subprocesses and are an order of magnitude slower. Under CI contention the slowest of those is the one that crosses 30s, and with no retry, crossing it once is sufficient to fail the pipeline.\n\n## Why the diagnosis path makes this worse\n\nThe shard's console output ends at \"blob report written to .vitest-reports/blob-1.json\" and \"Process completed with exit code 1\". The failing test name is present in the raw log but there is no job summary carrying it, so the practical route to a diagnosis is `gh run view --log-failed` and stripping ANSI escapes, or downloading and decoding the blob artifact. That cost is paid on every red shard regardless of cause, which is precisely the pressure that makes \"rerun and see\" the rational first move.\n\n## Base rate, stated honestly\n\nAcross the last 14 CI runs on main this is the only failure; the two other non-successes were cancellations. So the recurrence rate is not established and this item should not claim the test is chronically flaky. What is established is the policy gap: there is no mechanism that would distinguish a transient timeout from a real failure if it did recur, and no record that would let anyone compute the rate. That is the thing to fix, independently of how often this particular test crosses its budget.\n\n## Boundary\n\nRaising `testTimeout` globally is not the fix. It would hide the at-risk tests rather than report them, and it lengthens the feedback loop for every genuine hang. The fix is bounded retry with the retry recorded, plus a report of tests whose observed cost approaches their budget."
